  "output": "`compute_norms.py` is written and verified. It reads `config.json` for `num_clients`, loads each `clientN.json`, and prints the raw L2 norm of each update vector.\n\nOutput from the actual run:\n\n```\nclient1: 0.866025   # √(0.75)\nclient2: 1.732051   # √3\nclient3: 2.000000   # √4\n```\n\nSanity check: with a clipping bound of 1.5 (from your config), client2 and client3 will need clipping while client1 stays as-is — the norms line up exactly as expected.",
